35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission trial worked, but the shared nursing round failed due to access issues.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system misses unlogged work, and our physical capacity is already maxed out.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic closed because neither department wanted the burden. Data agreements are slow.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Nursing vacancies are high, and agency costs are rising. Midwifery has unexpected slack.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The budget is down a quarter, and off-site visits generate no revenue. This is tight.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we justify a home follow-up team?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, that is a valid point. The financial model for home visits is weak.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the midwifery slack is interesting. Could we leverage that for a new service?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, yes, but we must ensure it does not strain the already thin nursing ranks.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, the booking system gap means we might not even see the activity we fund.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data suggests home visits work, but the funding model is broken.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We need a program that fits within existing on-site capacity to ensure billing.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,A perinatal service could use the midwifery slack and stay on-site for billing.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I agree. It avoids the agency cost trap and utilizes available staff.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,On-site billing is crucial given the tariff rules. This seems financially safer.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards the perinatal option. It has staff availability and billing potential.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,It fits the physical constraints better than home visits or new outpatient rooms.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It avoids the joint management trap that killed the previous clinic.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,It uses the midwifery slack without adding pressure to the nursing vacancies.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,It maximizes revenue per unit of budget. I support this direction.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
